{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>עני</b> — the meaning: from the days of youth his constitution was not strong; he was like one dying, though I was poor I bore your terror, and the meaning is <i>the ailments</i>." "<b>And the word אפונה</b> — from the root of פן, like אעלה from the root of על, and תהינו from the root of הנה." "<b>And the meaning of אגורה</b> — and I fear."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 88, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is terse and compressed; 'תולדתו חזקה' reads literally as 'his generation/constitution [was] strong'; the clause 'והטעם החליים' appears to re-gloss עני as 'ailments' (related to חולי), though the logical connection to the preceding argument is not made explicit."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:24.924031502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}